locate.c — Geany Find File Plugin
==================================

Single-file GTK plugin for Geany that wraps the OS ``locate`` command.

Source layout
-------------

.. list-table::
   :header-rows: 1
   :widths: 35 65

   * - Symbol
     - Purpose
   * - ``gl_init`` / ``gl_cleanup``
     - Plugin lifecycle — register menu items, keybinding, key-press hook
   * - ``locate_dialog_show``
     - Build and present the Find File dialog (idempotent)
   * - ``locate_run_search``
     - Assemble argv, spawn ``locate`` as a ``GSubprocess``, kick off async read
   * - ``on_read_line_done``
     - ``GDataInputStream`` async callback — collects lines into ``GPtrArray``
   * - ``locate_async_finish``
     - Called at EOF or error; dispatches to one of the three result modes
   * - ``result_none``
     - 0 matches — update status label, leave dialog open
   * - ``result_one``
     - 1 match — show path in dialog, pressing Enter opens the file
   * - ``result_many``
     - 2+ matches — populate Messages tab, close dialog
   * - ``locate_populate_messages``
     - Writes relative paths to the Messages tab as clickable links
   * - ``build_locate_argv``
     - Constructs ``locate [-i] -r ^<root>.*<query>`` argv
   * - ``on_key_press``
     - Double-tap Shift detection (300 ms window)
   * - ``on_updatedb_activate``
     - Runs ``sudo updatedb`` via geanycli signal or ``g_spawn_command_line_async``

Menu placement
--------------

Geany's plugin API only exposes ``GeanyMainWidgets.tools_menu``; there is no
``search_menu`` in the public surface.  Both "Find File" and "updatedb" are
therefore added to the Tools menu.

Async search lifecycle
----------------------

::

    locate_run_search()
      └─ g_subprocess_newv()          ← spawns locate
      └─ g_data_input_stream_read_line_async()
            │  (repeated per line)
            └─ on_read_line_done()
                  └─ locate_async_finish()   ← on EOF or error
                        └─ result_none / result_one / result_many

A ``GCancellable`` (``search_cancel``) is replaced on each new search so an
in-flight read is cancelled before the next one starts.

Requirements
------------

``mlocate`` or ``plocate`` must be installed (``locate`` on ``$PATH``).
